# fde-03-evaluation

The starting point for every repo in the **Forward Deployed ML Engineer: Zero-to-Hired** series. Each phase repo (`fde-00` to `fde-07`) is created from this template, so all of them share one structure, one quality bar and one deployment matrix: **Docker Desktop, Podman Desktop and Rancher Desktop locally, AWS, Azure and GCP in the cloud**, plus Kubernetes, OpenShift and Helm.

The template runs as-is: a small FastAPI service with health checks, Prometheus metrics, a provider-agnostic LLM client (Mistral by default; OpenAI, DeepSeek, Qwen, Kimi or self-hosted by configuration), and an end-to-end smoke test that every deployment path must pass.

## Create a phase repo from this template

```bash
gh repo create sundayayandele/fde-00-programming --template sundayayandele/fde-03-evaluation --public --clone
cd fde-00-programming
python scripts/init_repo.py --repo fde-00-programming --package complaints_ingest
make install && make test && make e2e
```

Then replace the hello endpoint with the phase's system, fill in `docs/`, write the weekly `labs/`, and wrap each learner exercise in solution markers (see [Reference and starter repos](#reference-and-starter-repos)).

## Run it

| Path | Command | What it proves |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Local Python | `make install && make e2e` | Code, tests and smoke checks |
| Docker Desktop | `make up-docker` | Container image and Compose stack |
| Podman Desktop | `make up-podman` (pod) or `make up-podman-compose` | Rootless containers, Kubernetes-style pod spec |
| Rancher Desktop | `make up-rancher` | Same stack on Rancher's dockerd (moby) engine |
| Local Kubernetes | `make k8s-docker`, `make k8s-rancher`, `make k8s-kind` | Manifests, probes, security context |
| OpenShift | `make k8s-openshift`, then `oc apply -k deploy/openshift` | Route and arbitrary-UID compatibility |
| AWS / Azure / GCP | `make tf-aws-plan` (and `azure`, `gcp`) | Terraform lab stacks with USD 50 monthly budget alerts |

Step-by-step labs, sizing and troubleshooting: [desktop labs](docs/learning/DESKTOP-LABS.md) and [cloud labs](docs/learning/CLOUD-LABS.md). Run `make help` for every target.

## Results

The template has no model, so its "results" are the gates every phase repo must pass:

| Gate | Evidence |
| --- | --- |
| Unit and API tests | `make test`, coverage gate 80% |
| End-to-end | `make e2e` locally; `e2e` workflow runs process, Compose and kind |
| Security | `security` workflow: pip-audit, gitleaks, Trivy (dependencies, secrets, image) |
| Infrastructure as code | `iac` workflow: fmt, validate, tflint for AWS, Azure, GCP |
| Manifests | `manifests` workflow: renders base, 3 desktop overlays, cloud, OpenShift, Helm; kubeconform |

## Repository map

```text
app/                 FastAPI service (health, metrics, API)
src/rag_eval/     package: config, provider-agnostic LLM client
config/              providers.yaml (Mistral default; OpenAI, DeepSeek, Qwen, Kimi, self-hosted)
scripts/             init_repo, make_starter, smoke_test, check_structure
tests/               unit, API, starter-generator and structure tests; e2e/smoke.yaml
evals/               evaluation harness and committed results (phase repos)
labs/                one folder per curriculum week
docs/                architecture, ADRs, customer, security, MLOps, datasets, infra, learning, TCO
diagrams/source/     Mermaid sources (rendered in CI)
deploy/              compose, podman, kubernetes (base + overlays), openshift, helm, gpu
terraform/           aws, azure, gcp lab stacks
monitoring/          Prometheus, alerts, Grafana
.github/workflows/   ci, e2e, security, iac, manifests, diagrams, evals, publish-starter
```

## Reference and starter repos

Every phase has a **reference repo** (complete solution, measured results) and a generated **starter repo** for learners. Wrap each exercise in the reference code:

```python
def greet(name: str) -> str:
    # >>> SOLUTION: week-00 hello endpoint
    return f"Hello, {name.strip()}!"
    # <<< SOLUTION
```

`scripts/make_starter.py` replaces each block with a `NotImplementedError("TODO ...")` stub, blanks marked Markdown sections, drops paths in `.starterignore`, and the `publish-starter` workflow pushes the result to `<repo>-starter` on every release tag. Exercise tests carry `@pytest.mark.exercise`; starter CI skips them, learners run `make exercises`.

